    <!-- ==================================================================
         01. HERO / LANDING SECTION
         ================================================================== -->
  
  <main class="archive-content">
    <section id="landing" class="archive-section">
      <br><br><br>
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-content">
          <h1 class="hero-title">DAC-ian Era</h1>
          <div class="hero-subtitle">FIELD INSTRUMENT // Artifact : Elie-Reader</div>
          
          <p class="hero-intro">
            A world where digital memory has dissolved into physical matter. 
          </p>

          <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 48ch; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            A Speculative Exploration of a plausible future As part of studio curriculum <br> Masters of Design in Human Centerd Design
          </p>

         <!--<p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 48ch; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            Recovered from a world where digital memory has dissolved into physical matter. 
            The READER translates buried electromagnetic, acoustic, and hydrological residue 
            into perceptible frequency, vibration, and cymatic form.
          </p>-->

          <!--<div class="hero-cta-group">
            <a href="http://localhost:8787/laptop/" class="btn-primary js-enter-sim-btn">
              ENTER THE FIELD →
            </a>
            <a href="#" class="btn-secondary" data-target="the-world">
              BEGIN WITH THE GUIDE ↓
            </a>
          </div>-->
        </div>

        <!-- Hero Oscilloscope / Signal Trace Frame -->
        <div class="hero-instrument-box">
          <div class="instrument-screen-top">
            <span>OSCILLOSCOPE // TRACE 01</span>
            <span id="signal-state-display" style="color: var(--accent-cyan);">RESONANCE LOCKED [WATER]</span>
          </div>

          <div class="oscilloscope-canvas-wrapper">
            <canvas id="hero-oscilloscope" class="oscilloscope-canvas"></canvas>
            <div class="oscilloscope-grid-overlay"></div>
          </div>

          <div class="instrument-screen-bottom">
            <span>BASE: <strong id="freq-val-display" style="color:#fff;">240 HZ</strong></span>
            <span>BAND: <strong style="color:#fff;">80HZ - 120 HZ</strong></span>
            <span>DAC/04: <strong style= "color:#fff;">Elie-Reader</strong></span>
            <!--<span>COUPLING: <strong>HAPTIC-ACOUSTIC</strong></span>-->
          </div>

          <div class="interactive-tuner-slider">
            <label for="freq-tuner-input">SWEEP FREQUENCY:</label>
            <input type="range" id="freq-tuner-input" min="80" max="1200" value="440" step="1">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         02. THE WORLD (DACIANS & SPECULATIVE FRAGMENTS)
         ================================================================== -->
    <section id="the-world" class="archive-section">
      <br><br><br>

      <div class="section-archival-header">
        <div class="section-meta-header">
          <span class="section-num">02 // SPECULATIVE WORLD</span>
          <div class="section-line"></div>
          <span class="archival-badge">ANTHROPOLOGICAL DOSSIER</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="section-title">The World of the DACians</h2>
        <p class="section-tagline">
          In a future where information has returned to the physical, signals are not stored in servers—they are found, repaired, and remembered.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-2col" style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem;">
        <div>
          <p class="world-lead-text">
            The DACians belong to an era in which digital information has become increasingly 
            analogue, physical, repairable, and ephemeral. They do not maintain disembodied cloud servers. 
            Instead, memory is understood as something suspended inside silt, trapped between quartz crystals, 
            or lingering in the acoustic resonance of old foundations.
          </p>

          <div class="field-fragment-quote">
            “The DACians do not separate information from the materials that carry it.”
            <span class="field-fragment-author">OBSERVATION LOG // DAC-WORLD ARCHIVE</span>
          </div>

          <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">
            In this world, a message is not broadcast outward across fiber optic wires; it is deposited into 
            an environment. A researcher must travel into the field with sensitive physical transducers 
            to physically meet the signal at its point of resting.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="archival-plate">
            <div class="plate-header">
              <span class="plate-title">TENETS OF DACIAN SIGNAL ECOLOGY</span>
              <span class="plate-index">DOC // REF-08</span>
            </div>

            <ul style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem;">
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.92rem;">
                <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent-rust); font-weight: 700;">[01]</span>
                <div>
                  <strong>SIGNALS ARE FOUND, NOT TRANSMITTED</strong>
                  <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: 0.25rem;">Information does not seek the user. The user must calibrate their physical instrument to the frequency of the ground.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.92rem;">
                <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent-rust); font-weight: 700;">[02]</span>
                <div>
                  <strong>DAMAGE IS NOT LOSS</strong>
                  <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: 0.25rem;">A corrupted signal is not deleted or thrown away. It simply requires tactile mending and human presence to restore.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.92rem;">
                <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent-rust); font-weight: 700;">[03]</span>
                <div>
                  <strong>THE READER AS MEDIATOR</strong>
                  <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: 0.25rem;">The READER does not originate thoughts; it acts as a mechanical lens extending human sensory perception into the invisible realm.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Fragment Cards -->
      <div class="fragment-grid">
        <div class="fragment-card">
          <div class="fragment-badge">FIELD FRAGMENT // 01</div>
          <div class="fragment-body">
            “Signals are not simply transmitted. They are found, tuned, interpreted, and repaired.”
          </div>
          <div class="fragment-meta">
            <span>COLLECTED BY [CREATOR]</span>
            <span>SAMPLE: HYDRO-01</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fragment-card">
          <div class="fragment-badge">FIELD FRAGMENT // 02</div>
          <div class="fragment-body">
            “A damaged signal is not necessarily lost. It may simply require another way of listening.”
          </div>
          <div class="fragment-meta">
            <span>COLLECTED BY [CREATOR]</span>
            <span>SAMPLE: SILT-04</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fragment-card">
          <div class="fragment-badge">FIELD FRAGMENT // 03</div>
          <div class="fragment-body">
            “The instrument speaks through sound, vibration, and frequency proximity before words emerge.”
          </div>
          <div class="fragment-meta">
            <span>COLLECTED BY [CREATOR]</span>
            <span>SAMPLE: RESIDUE-09</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Material Matrix -->
      <div class="material-matrix">
        <div class="material-node">
          <div class="material-num">SUBSTRATE // A</div>
          <div class="material-name">Aqueous Silt</div>
          <div class="material-desc">
            Submerged particles that trap deep acoustic low-pass tones. Resonates around 440 Hz in calm water.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="material-node">
          <div class="material-num">SUBSTRATE // B</div>
          <div class="material-name">Quartz Residue</div>
          <div class="material-desc">
            Shifting granular sand that generates high dry friction. Retains high-frequency vocal formants at 520 Hz.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="material-node">
          <div class="material-num">SUBSTRATE // C</div>
          <div class="material-name">Alloy Filament</div>
          <div class="material-desc">
            Thin conductive veins woven through ancient masonry. Requires continuous manual touch to mend.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="material-node">
          <div class="material-num">SUBSTRATE // D</div>
          <div class="material-name">The Cymatic Medium</div>
          <div class="material-desc">
            Fluid or particle surfaces that rearrange under acoustic pressure to reveal geometric patterns.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         03. WHAT IS THE READER?
         ================================================================== -->
    <section id="artifact" class="archive-section">
      <!--<span class="corner-reg tl">+</span>
      <span class="corner-reg tr">+</span>-->
      <br><br><br>

      <div class="section-archival-header">
        <div class="section-meta-header">
          <span class="section-num">03 // INSTRUMENT SPECIFICATION</span>
          <div class="section-line"></div>
          <span class="archival-badge alert">FIELD HARDWARE</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="section-title">What is the READER?</h2>
        <p class="section-tagline">
          The READER is a field instrument used to locate and interpret signals embedded within an environment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        The system relies on a dual-apparatus interaction model: a stationary monitoring receiver 
        and an agile handheld instrument held in the field researcher's palm. Together, they form 
        a closed loop between observation, resonance tuning, and physical repair.
      </p>

      <!-- Interactive Instrument Topology Diagram -->
      <div class="topology-diagram-container">
        <div class="plate-header">
          <span class="plate-title">SYSTEM TOPOLOGY // TRANSMISSION & SENSORY INTERPRETATION</span>
          <span class="plate-index">SCHEMATIC DAC-04-T</span>
        </div>

        <div class="topology-schematic">
          <!-- Node 1: Field Receiver -->
          <div class="topology-node active-field">
            <div class="topology-node-icon">💻</div>
            <div class="topology-node-title">FIELD RECEIVER</div>
            <div class="archival-badge" style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">LAPTOP STATION</div>
            <p class="topology-node-desc">
              Visual monitoring terminal. Renders real-time cymatic particle physics, monitors network telemetry, and records the researcher’s observation log.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Arrow 1 -->
          <div class="topology-arrow">
            <span>TRANSMISSION</span>
            <div class="topology-arrow-line"></div>
            <span>SIGNAL</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Node 2: Handheld Reader -->
          <div class="topology-node active-field">
            <div class="topology-node-icon">📱</div>
            <div class="topology-node-title">READER</div>
            <div class="archival-badge alert" style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">HANDHELD INSTRUMENT</div>
            <p class="topology-node-desc">
              Phone-based sensor. Sweeps frequency spectrum, emits buried acoustic layers, pulses with haptic vibration, and executes the MEND interaction.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Arrow 2 -->
          <div class="topology-arrow">
            <span>FREQUENCY</span>
            <div class="topology-arrow-line"></div>
            <span>SENSORY CUES</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Node 3: User Perception -->
          <div class="topology-node">
            <div class="topology-node-icon">👁️👂✋</div>
            <div class="topology-node-title">FIELD RESEARCHER</div>
            <div class="archival-badge" style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">PERCEPTION & TOUCH</div>
            <p class="topology-node-desc">
              The human interpreter. Listens for buried phrases, feels for frequency proximity, locates the fillámend, and records qualitative field notes.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Instrument Comparison Specifications -->
      <div class="instrument-spec-grid">
        <div class="spec-column archival-plate">
          <h4>FIELD RECEIVER (LAPTOP)</h4>
          <div class="spec-list">
            <div class="spec-item">
              <span class="spec-label">Primary Role</span>
              <span class="spec-value">Stationary Monitor & Archive</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-item">
              <span class="spec-label">Visual Field</span>
              <span class="spec-value">Dynamic Cymatic Particle Canvas</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-item">
              <span class="spec-label">Telemetry Readout</span>
              <span class="spec-value">Live Frequency, Band, & Status</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-item">
              <span class="spec-label">Observation Sink</span>
              <span class="spec-value">Permanent Field Log Record</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spec-column archival-plate">
          <h4>READER (HANDHELD SMARTPHONE)</h4>
          <div class="spec-list">
            <div class="spec-item">
              <span class="spec-label">Primary Role</span>
              <span class="spec-value">Mobile Sensor & Tuning Probe</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-item">
              <span class="spec-label">Sensory Output</span>
              <span class="spec-value">WebAudio Layers & Haptic Vibration</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-item">
              <span class="spec-label">Controls</span>
              <span class="spec-value">Flow (Freq), Depth (Band), Listen, Mend</span>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-item">
              <span class="spec-label">Input Mechanism</span>
              <span class="spec-value">On-Screen Archival QWERTY Keypad</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

